WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.620
Marvel's own God of Mischief-centered series
"Loki" just wrapped up its freshman season,

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.260
and fans have loved the time-bending thrill
ride.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:12.690
Nicely connected to other films in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe, set after the events of

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:17.940
"Avengers: Endgame," "Loki" adds additional
layers to the already complex world of heroes

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:23.090
and villains, and the season finale reveals
just enough information to get fans excited

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.910
about "Loki" Season 2.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:30.000
The sixth and final episode of Season 1 finds
Loki and Sylvie reaching the Citadel at the

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.070
End of Time, and by the end of the episode,
they meet a major Marvel villain: the enigmatic

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:40.550
He Who Remains, a variant of Kang the Konquerer
whom Sylvie ends up murdering after shoving

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:42.350
Loki through a portal.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:46.940
Perhaps more surprisingly, one of the loyal
subjects to He Who Remains is identified at

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:51.300
the very beginning of the episode, and it's
a reveal many fans had theorized about since

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.700
the start of "Loki."

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:58.280
One of the newer characters introduced to
the MCU in "Loki" is Miss Minutes, an animated

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:03.930
anthropomorphic clock who serves as both an
assistant and mascot of the Time Variance

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:04.930
Authority.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:09.691
Her sweet southern drawl and emphasis on manners
and rules may seem wholesome at first, but

00:01:09.691 --> 00:01:14.430
many fans had a lingering feeling that she
isn't as innocent as she appears.

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:16.970
And as it turns out, those fans were correct.

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:21.690
In the first few moments of the Season 1 finale,
Loki and Sylvie are greeted by the creepily

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:26.550
cheerful Miss Minutes, who reveals her loyalty
to He Who Remains and her behind-the-scenes

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.370
workings with the TVA.

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:33.220
While each "Loki" episode usually sends the
internet into a frenzy anyway, this final

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:37.200
episode lit up social media even more thanks
to its big reveals.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.340
Tons of fans took to Twitter to joke about
how creepy Miss Minutes was in her initial

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.880
jump scare, likening her to a horror movie
monster.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.150
One Twitter user wrote that they didn't see
the Miss Minutes reveal coming, though there

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:52.680
have been fan theories about her true evil
nature floating around the internet as early

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.400
as June, according to sites like Inverse.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:59.450
Whether you saw this reveal coming or not,
the Season 1 finale of "Loki" has opened the

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:04.130
doors for many more exciting adventures in
Season 2, and we can't wait to see what happens

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:05.229
next.

00:02:05.229 --> 00:02:09.580
After the reveal that Miss Minutes is actually
an important henchmen to the two Big Bads

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:14.450
of "Loki" — Kang and Renslayer — fans
were left shocked that this cheerful, animated

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:16.750
character was a bad guy in disguise.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:21.700
However, Miss Minutes is still a pretty fascinating
character, thanks to her top-notch animation

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:26.700
and Tara Strong's excellent vocal performance
— and since the MCU loves bringing back

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:32.070
popular characters, it's definitely possible
that this cute TVA mascot may pop up in future

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.660
Marvel films and television shows.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:38.459
According to an interview on Marvel's own
website, Miss Minutes was a favorite amongst

00:02:38.459 --> 00:02:42.920
the show's creators as well as its fans, which
meant that the creative team behind "Loki"

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:46.700
cooked up ways to keep her as involved in
the narrative as possible.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:48.370
Director Kate Herron revealed,

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:52.920
"Early on in the scripts, we all were definitely
united on, 'We've got to keep Miss Minutes

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.430
in the story somehow.'"

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:56.720
Head writer Michael Waldron agreed, saying,

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:00.340
"She was a really fun way to deliver some
pretty heady exposition.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:03.730
There's something sing-songy and sort of non-threatening
about [the way she talks].

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:07.820
But yet, when it turns, and when she becomes
evil, suddenly it's really scary."

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:12.470
In fact, Miss Minutes originally had even
more to do, as Waldron explained, including

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:16.099
a daring fight scene — which, sadly, hit
the cutting room floor.

00:03:16.099 --> 00:03:19.690
Waldron told Marvel that the show's writers
crafted Miss Minutes as a character that would

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:20.690
serve as,

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:24.670
"That devil on the shoulder and trying to
tempt both Loki and Sylvie.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:28.180
It was fun that you got a sense of there's
something a bit more sinister going on here

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.180
with her."

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.470
He also revealed a scene that ultimately never
came to pass:

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:35.620
"We always had a version where [Loki and Sylvie]
kept meeting her at the Citadel.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:39.370
At one point, we had a fight scene with Miss
Minutes in the Citadel; we had all kinds of

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:40.459
stuff [for her]."

00:03:40.459 --> 00:03:44.540
The first season of "Loki" is streaming in
its entirety on Disney Plus now.

